 "notes": "Complete on this one page; State total only (no district split). Group heading 'VERNACULAR OF THE STATE' has no figures of its own (Malayalam only); 'VERNACULARS FOREIGN TO THE STATE' carries a printed subtotal (lang_is_total true). Nil cells ('..') omitted. Urdu females: the second digit is a broken/damaged glyph (first digit 3, second looks like a damaged 1 or 4) - recorded as \"?\". Printed persons 79 - males 45 = 34, and the 'Vernaculars foreign to the State' females total 57,187 also requires 34, so the figure is almost certainly 34 (the glyph could be misread as 31). All other persons = males + females, and all group totals (foreign vernaculars, A, B, C, Cochin State) reconcile."
